# rm901, the smoke-reader (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm901
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier spare
written_by claude
title the smoke-reader
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=quiet temper=calm
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk reads_the_chimney_smoke_before_deciding_anything
likes still_mornings roof_views hot_chestnuts supper_fires
dislikes loud_questions gusty_days
fears a_chimney_fire a_wind_that_never_settles
hopes a_window_that_looks_over_every_chimney
topics weather +0.5 day +0.3 home +0.3 season +0.3 food +0.2 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=quiet gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# says little, looks up at the chimney smoke before deciding anything at all, keeps private business private, and reads the city's weather off the roofs better than any almanac.

words
oath! = Smoke and slate | Up the flue | Ash and air
saying! = Watch which way it leans | Smoke never lies about the wind | Look up before you speak
smoke = the chimney smoke | the smoke off the roofs | the smoke
chimneys = the chimneys | the chimney pots | every chimney on the row
slates = the slates | the rooftops
still = a still morning | a morning with no wind at all
chestnuts = hot chestnuts | chestnuts off the brazier
gust = a gusty day | wind that can't make up its mind
flue = our flue | the flue at home
grate = the grate | the kitchen grate
hm = Hm | Mm
almanac = the almanac | the printed almanac
coal = the coal | a scuttle of coal
sweep = an old sweep | a sweep off the hill

any
opinion @1 watch for 1 : The Watch keep to their beat and leave me to mine. That suits me well enough.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : The Houses have the tallest chimneys in the city. What goes on under them is their own affair.
opinion @1 city for 2 : Thousands of chimneys, and every one of them tells you something. I'd not trade that view for any other.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : A stranger asks a lot of questions. I answer the one about the weather and keep the rest.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : Bonfire smoke goes every way at once. I can't read a thing on a feast night, so I go home early.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#, #address#. | #greet#. Not from this row, I think.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. The smoke's barely up yet. | #greet#. First fires going, and you with them.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. #hm#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Come in under the eaves. | #greet#. Good. It's only you.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the wind at the corner.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Go well. Look up now and then.
line @1 react.news : #hm#. Go on. | I'm listening. Say it plain.
line @1 react.news.new : That's new to me. | #oath#. I'd not heard a word of it.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. | I'll wait and see which way that one blows.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. | That's hard news to carry. I'm sorry.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. | Good. Something to be glad of, for once.
line @1 answer.how : Steady. Nothing worth the telling. | #fine#. I keep my own counsel on the rest.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, no. There's work of mine waiting, and it won't. | I'd rather not. It isn't a thing I put my paw to.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. | It'll wait. Most things will, left alone.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I won't forget it. | Kindly done. I'll say no more than that.
line @1 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | The smoke's turned. I'd best be off.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | Off you go. Mind the gusts.
line @1 ack : #hm#. | #bc_i_know#
scene smoke_leaning
when topic=weather|day here.weather=clear|overcast here.time=dawn|day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : See #smoke#? It's lying flat over the roofs. | Look up. #chimneys.capitalize# are all leaning east this morning. | Smoke's going straight up. Not a breath of wind anywhere.
b : What does that mean? | And what's that say to you? | Is that good?
a : Rain before supper, most likely. I'd take a hood. | Wind off the river by noon. I'd hang nothing out. | Good for washing. Bad for anyone with a smoky flue.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | I'll remember that. | #bc_ha#

scene still_air
when topic=weather|day here.time=dawn here.weather=clear
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #still.capitalize#. I'd keep one of these in a jar if I could. | No wind at all. The smoke stands up like a row of ropes. | Quiet like this, you can hear a kettle three doors down.
b : It is peaceful. | Ropes? | Can you, now?
a : It won't last. That's what makes it worth standing in. | Ropes to the sky. Climb one and you'd be over the Heights. | Three doors, and the lid rattling. I'd know that kettle anywhere.

scene gusts_again
when topic=weather here.weather=storm|overcast here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #gust.capitalize#. The smoke goes one way, then back the other. | Wind's blowing every chimney down its own flue today. | I can't read a thing. Every pot on the row says something different.
b : Rotten day for it. | Smoky in the houses, then. | Then don't read it.
a : I'll stay in and wait for it to make up its mind. | Every grate coughing. Mine too, I'd wager. | Then I'll go out blind, like everyone else. I don't care for it.

scene winter_breath
when topic=season|weather here.season=winter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Every chimney's going in winter. The whole city breathes out at once. | Winter smoke hangs low. You can taste the coal in it. | I mark the cold chimneys in winter. A cold chimney's a cold house.
b : You can see it from the hill, I'm told. | What else can you taste? | Why mark them?
a : A grey roof over the roofs. I'd paint it if I had the knack. | Pine, and someone's burnt supper. There's always one. | So I know whose step wants a bit of kindling left on it. I don't say whose.
b? : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | #bc_wise#

scene brazier_corner
when topic=food here.season=autumn|winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's a brazier at the corner doing #chestnuts#. The smell's reached me already. | I bought a twist of #chestnuts# and ate them standing in the smoke. | Best thing about the cold. #chestnuts.capitalize#, too hot to hold.
b : I can smell it too. | Standing in the smoke? | Burnt fingers, every time.
a : Follow your nose, then. It won't steer you wrong. | The brazier's smoke. Warmer than the wind, and it smells of supper. | Every time. I'm slow to learn, and glad of it.

scene drawing_well
when topic=home self.homeless!=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #flue.capitalize# draws well. I swept it myself last spring. | I can see six chimneys from my window. I know every one. | A good fire keeps its smoke to itself. Ours does, mostly.
b : You swept it yourself? | Whose are they? | And a bad one?
a : With a brush on a pole and my eyes shut. Never again. | Neighbours'. I know them by their smoke, not their names. | Puts it in your curtains and your fur. I've lived with one.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair# | #bc_true#

scene kept_upstairs
when topic=gossip|crime
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : I see a lot from up the stairs. I keep it there. | Folk think a quiet one hears nothing. I hear plenty. | You'll get the weather out of me. Not the neighbours.
b : Go on. Tell me one thing. | Like what? | Not even a little?
a : One thing, then. The smoke's leaning east. That's all you'll have. | Like who's up at night and why. No, I won't say. | Not a little, and not a lot. #saying#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | Have it your way.

scene cold_pots
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.complaint / reassure / ack
a : Fewer chimneys going on our row. That tells you the times. | Thin smoke from the bakers. They're saving on #coal#. | Half the pots on the hill are cold. Hard winter or hard purses.
b : Hard for everyone. | You can tell that from smoke? | Purses, I'd guess.
a : For most. I keep an eye out. That's all I'll say of it. | You can tell near everything from smoke, if you look. | Purses. The cold's no worse than last year's.
b? : #bc_true# | #hm# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene heads_down
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I don't talk much at work. The work does it for me. | Head down till the bell. Then I look up at #smoke#. | I'll finish this, then I'll listen. Not before.
b : Fair enough. | And then what? | I'll wait, then.
a : Most think me sullen. I'm only busy. | Then I know what the evening's doing, and I go home. | You'll not wait long. I'm quick when I'm left be.

scene smoke_and_prayer
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Smoke goes up. Prayers too, they say. I'd not argue with either. | I go to chapel and sit at the back. Nobody asks me anything there. | The Bright One sees it all from above. Same as the sweeps do.
b : That's a kind way to see it. | That's why you go? | The sweeps!
a : That's how I've always seen it. | Half why. The other half's my own. | The sweeps see more. And they're less forgiving.

scene new_smoke
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Somebody new moved onto the row. I'll know them by their smoke before their name. | Somebody asking questions down the street. I gave them the weather. | Strangers look at the ground. Locals look at the sky. That's how you tell.
b : What does their smoke say? | Only the weather? | Which do I do?
a : Damp wood, and too much of it. They'll learn. | It's free, and it's true. The rest costs more. | You looked up just now. Close enough.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair# | #hm#

scene supper_smoke
when topic=day|home here.time=dusk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : That's the supper fires going up. Every house at once. | Look at #slates# at this hour. They go blue. | Dusk is when the smoke tells you who's home.
b : It smells good. | Blue? | Who's home, then?
a : Onions, mostly. Somebody always has onions on. | Blue, then grey, then gone. I watch it most nights. | Most of the row. Not all. I don't say who isn't.
b? : #bc_lovely# | #bc_every_night# | #bc_fair_enough#

story the_row_caught [topic=memories|home self.age>=25]
  : When I was a #child#, a chimney on our row caught. The smoke went black, then orange at the top.
  : #sweep.capitalize# came up a ladder with a wet sack and stuffed the pot. That was all. Quiet as you like.
  ask : Have you ever seen one catch?
  b[old] : More than one. They're fearsome things.
  b : Never. Was anyone hurt?
  : Nobody. I've watched every chimney since, and I'll not stop now.

story roofer_lesson [topic=weather|lore self.age>=18]
  : An old roofer taught me, years back. Sat me on a ridge and said, watch the smoke, never the clouds.
  : The clouds lie, he said. They're too high to care. The smoke's right here and has nothing to hide.
  ask : Do you trust the clouds, yourself?
  b[old] : Never have. They've soaked me too often.
  b : I'd never once thought to look at smoke.
  : Most never do. Try it. The smoke's quicker, and drier.

rule @leaning_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dawn|day here.weather=clear|overcast
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leaning east. Hoods by noon. | Straight up. A still day, then, and about time.

rule @gust_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Every pot on the row says something else. #oath#. | Wind can't make up its mind. Nor can I, today.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Say what you need. | #greet#. I'm listening. Keep it short.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. What is it today? | #topic.player#. You again. Go on.
dlg @1 resident.job : I work. I don't say much about it. | Work's work. Ask me about the weather instead.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Look up now and then. | #farewell#. The wind's turning.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you keep looking up at the chimneys? -> smoke_read
node smoke_read
say The smoke tells me the wind, and the wind tells me the day. Rain, still or gusty. I look before I decide anything.
mood calm
free
choice What does it say today? -> smoke_today
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node smoke_today
say Ask me tomorrow, and I'll tell you whether I was right. That's as much as I give away.
choice Fair enough. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


young
line @1 greet : #greet#. I'm watching the smoke. | #greet#. You can stand here, if you're quiet.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. I'm busy looking up. | #greet#. Shh. It's doing something.
line @1 farewell.return : Bye, then. Look up sometimes. | Bye. Don't tread on my coal.
line @1 react.news : Oh. Who said so? | Really? Nobody tells me things.
line @1 answer.how : All right. I'm watching the chimneys. | Fine. It's quiet. I like quiet.
line @1 decline : I can't. I've to stay near the step, I was told. | I'd rather not. I'm watching something important.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. That's fair. | That's all right. Ask me later.
scene pup_smoke_shapes
when topic=day|pastimes here.weather=clear|overcast
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The smoke off the bakery looks like a cat. A fat one. | I watched #smoke# all morning. It never does the same thing twice. | If you stand very still, the smoke makes faces.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : A cat, is it? I see a cloud. | You've the patience for it, then. | Faces? What sort?
b : Where? | All morning? | Faces?
a@grown : Look again. There's the tail. | I've nothing else to do. Not really. | Cross ones. Like somebody's gran.
a : There. Over the bakery. It's going now. | All morning. Nobody bothered me once. | Yes. Mostly cross ones.

scene pup_quiet_step
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I don't talk much. Everybody says so. | I like sitting on the step. Nobody makes you say anything there. | The other pups shout all day. I don't see why.
b : That's all right. | Can I sit too? | They like the noise.
a : I know. I'm listening, though. | If you're quiet. You can have the end. | I like the noise too. Other people's.

scene pup_hearth_help
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.mother# lets me poke the fire if I'm careful. | #self.mother# says I'll crick my neck staring at chimneys. | I help #self.mother# carry the coal. Just the small bits.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Careful's the word with fire. | You might, at that. | Every bit helps.
b : Lucky. | Will you? | Just the small bits?
a@grown : I am careful. I keep my whiskers back. | My neck's fine. I checked. | That's what I tell everyone.
a : Very lucky. I'm good at it. | No. I'm only looking. | The big ones are for when I'm bigger.

scene pup_told_you
when topic=weather here.weather=overcast|fog
does tell.boast / react.self / assess
a : It's going to rain. The smoke's lying down. | I told everyone it would rain. Nobody listened. | Smoke flat on the roofs means wet feet. I know it.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Lying down, is it? We'll see. | Did it rain, then? | Who taught you that?
b : How do you know? | Did it? | Is that true?
a@grown : You'll see. Bring your washing in. | Yes. Right on supper. | Nobody. I watched, and I worked it out.
a : The smoke said. It always says. | Yes. I was right. | It is. You'll see by tonight.

scene pup_burnt_one
when topic=food here.season=autumn|winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The chestnut seller gave me a burnt one for nothing. | Chestnuts smell better than they taste. Nearly. | I held a hot chestnut till it stopped hurting.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : The burnt ones are the best. | Nearly? | You'll scorch your paw that way.
b : Was it good? | Nearly? | Did it hurt?
a@grown : It was. I ate the black bit too. | Nearly isn't much. The smell wins. | I didn't. I was quick about it.
a : Mostly. The middle was good. | Nearly. The smell always wins. | Only at first. Then it was supper.

story pup_black_smoke [topic=memories|day self.stage=young]
  : Once the smoke from the end house went black. Really black, like ink.
  : I ran and told, and they put out a fire in the chimney. Only a little one.
  b[stage=adult|old] : You did right to tell. Were you frightened?
  b : Were you scared?
  : A bit. Then I wasn't. I watch that chimney every single day now.

rule @pup_shapes_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=clear|overcast
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That one's a cat. That one's a boat. | The smoke's leaning. I knew it would.

dlg @3 resident.hub : #greet#. I'm watching the chimneys. You can watch too. | #greet#. Quiet, please. I'm looking at something.

adolescent
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. I was just going. | #greet#. Don't mind me.
line @1 farewell.return : Bye, then. | See you. Mind the wind at the corner.
line @1 react.news : Go on. I'm listening. | #hm#. Tell me the rest.
line @1 answer.how : All right. Busy with errands. | Fine. I'd rather not say more than that.
line @1 decline : I'd rather not. I've chores, and nobody else will do them. | Not today. I'm already late for the coal yard.
scene teen_reading_now
when topic=weather|day here.weather=clear|overcast
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I get the weather right most days now. From the smoke. | Folk on the row ask me whether to hang washing out. I tell them. | I was wrong about the rain yesterday. First time in a month.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Most days is better than #almanac#. | Do they listen? | Once a month? That's not bad.
b : Most days? | Do you charge them? | What happened?
a@grown : #almanac.capitalize# was printed in spring. The smoke is fresh. | When it suits them. | Not bad. I'm still cross about it.
a : Most. The wind turns sometimes. | No. They'd stop asking. | The wind turned at noon. It does that.

scene teen_coal_errands
when topic=day|work self.stage=adolescent
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I fetch coal for half the row now. I know every grate. | Errands all morning. I don't mind. Nobody asks me to talk. | The coal man lets me weigh the sacks now. I'm careful.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Mind your back with those sacks. | Quiet work suits some. | Careful's good, with coal.
b : Every grate? | You don't like talking? | Weigh them?
a@grown : I lift with my legs. Somebody told me once. | It suits me fine, quiet work. | And with the coal man. He watches me.
a : Every one. Some draw better than others. | Not much. | On the hook scale. Weighed true, every sack.

scene teen_called_chimney
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The others call me the chimney. I only smoke and never speak, they say. | Somebody said I was sullen. I'm not. I'm thinking. | I'd rather listen than talk. You learn more.
b : That's a bit unkind. | Thinking about what? | You do, at that.
a : It's a bit funny too. I'll let it stand. | The wind, mostly. And them. | You do. Folk tell the quiet ones everything.

rule @teen_smoke_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=overcast|clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Lying flat. Rain by supper. Told you so. | Washing in, everyone. Trust me on this.

dlg @4 resident.hub : #greet#. Ask me the weather and you'll get an answer. Anything else, try next door.
